# business-logic

- This is an online marketplace for hiring freelancers.
- The unique selling point of this marketplace is that it is a marketplace based on crypto. Which means that the user can pay the freelancers in crypto.
- We are aiming to create a simple and intuitive app UI that is easy to use for both the freelancers and the clients.
- This is a hybrid app that is built with Sveltekit and Capacitor.

# Design philosophy

- We are aiming to create a minimalistic and modern UI.
- To properly support mobile devices and their respected platforms we are using latest version of Daisy UI.
- We are using the Sveltekit framework to build the app. So the frontend is written in Svelte 5 Runes.
- In svelte 5 there is not on:click event it's changed to onclick. Same goes for other on: events. Always use $state() to create reactive variables.
- With this same codebase we will support multiple platforms like Android, iOS, and Web.
- We are using Tailwind CSS for styling.
- We will also use Storybook for component development.

# Tech stack

- Sveltekit
- Svelte 5 Runes
- Daisy UI
- Capacitor
- Tailwind CSS
- Storybook
- TypeScript
- Vite
- Vitest
- Bun

# Rules

- All new components should go in src/lib/components and be named like ExampleComponent.svelte unless otherwise specified.
- All new pages go in src/lib/routes
- All new utils go in src/lib/utils
- All new stories go in src/lib/stories
- All the state management should go in src/lib/states
- We are also using vitest for testing.
- Ignore /node_modules and follow .cursorignore file for other files to ignore.

# Project structure

- src/lib/components
- src/lib/routes
- src/lib/utils
- src/lib/stories
- src/lib/states
